e been stable all cycle could put the result in doubt.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Maura Healey (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Maura Healey seeks a second term as governor of Massachusetts, one of the most Democratic-leaning states in the country, against Republican Mike Minogue and independent Andrea James. Polling throughout 2026 has been remarkably consistent: recent surveys from Suffolk, UMass Amherst, UNH, and MassINC all show Healey leading by 16 to 25 points, and published aggregates put her advantage around 21 to 23 points. Minogue has campaigned on affordability and criticized the state's direction, but coverage notes that President Trump's standing in Massachusetts weighs on his campaign.\n\nEvery major race-rating outlet calls the contest Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets give Healey roughly a 95 percent chance of winning. An RNC-sponsored survey reportedly showed a tighter matchup, but partisan internal polls of that kind are treated with caution. The race remains firmly in Healey's favor heading into election day.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9961, "margin": 18.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9968, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9983, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9947, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9875, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9913, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9921, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9908, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9953, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9946, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9924, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9932, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9949, "margin": 18.5}